# WatchMark Privacy Policy

_Last updated: 2026-08-21_

WatchMark stores the alert email address, monitoring URL, selected CSS path, last observed value, refresh interval, and tutorial preference in Chrome local extension storage.

When a monitored value changes, WatchMark sends the alert email address and new value to the configured EmailJS service to deliver the email alert. Chrome notifications and the on-page alert are generated locally.

WatchMark does not sell personal information. Data remains in local Chrome storage until the user removes it or clears extension data. EmailJS may process data according to its own privacy policy and the production service configuration.

Users can stop monitoring at any time. Stopping removes the monitoring URL, selected element path, last value, and monitoring state. The saved alert email can be cleared by replacing it or clearing the extension's storage.

